backported>\n\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '1. a patch based on a newer version: \nFrom 79990cf5e7aded76d0c092c9f5ed31eb1c75e02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Marcin Szycik <marcin.szycik@linux.intel.com>\nDate: Mon, 24 Feb 2025 11:06:41 -0800\nSubject: [PATCH] ice: Fix deinitializing VF in error path\n\nIf ice_ena_vfs() fails after calling ice_create_vf_entries(), it frees\nall VFs without removing them from snapshot PF-VF mailbox list, leading\nto list corruption.\n\nReproducer:\n  devlink dev eswitch set $PF1_PCI mode switchdev\n  ip l s $PF1 up\n  ip l s $PF1 promisc on\n  sleep 1\n  echo 1 > /sys/class/net/$PF1/device/sriov_numvfs\n  sleep 1\n  echo 1 > /sys/class/net/$PF1/device/sriov_numvfs\n\nTrace (minimized):\n  list_add corruption. next->prev should be prev (ffff8882e241c6f0), but was 0000000000000000. (next=ffff888455da1330).\n  kernel BUG at lib/list_debug.c:29!\n  RIP: 0010:__list_add_valid_or_report+0xa6/0x100\n   ice_mbx_init_vf_info+0xa7/0x180 [ice]\n   ice_initialize_vf_entry+0x1fa/0x250 [ice]\n   ice_sriov_configure+0x8d7/0x1520 [ice]\n   ? __percpu_ref_switch_mode+0x1b1/0x5d0\n   ? __pfx_ice_sriov_configure+0x10/0x10 [ice]\n\nSometimes a KASAN report can be seen instead with a similar stack trace:\n  BUG: KASAN: use-after-free in __list_add_valid_or_report+0xf1/0x100\n\nVFs are added to this list in ice_mbx_init_vf_info(), but only removed\nin ice_free_vfs(). Move the removing to ice_free_vf_entries(), which is\nalso being called in other places where VFs are being removed (including\nice_free_vfs() itself).\n\nFixes: 8cd8a6b17d27 ("ice: move VF overflow message count into struct ice_mbx_vf_info")\nReported-by: Sujai Buvaneswaran <sujai.buvaneswaran@intel.com>\nCloses: https://lore.kernel.org/intel-wired-lan/PH0PR11MB50138B635F2E5CEB7075325D961F2@PH0PR11MB5013.namprd11.prod.outlook.com\nReviewed-by: Martyna Szapar-Mudlaw <martyna.szapar-mudlaw@linux.intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Marcin Szycik <marcin.szycik@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Simon Horman <horms@kernel.org>\nTested-by: Sujai Buvaneswaran <sujai.buvaneswaran@intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Tony Nguyen <anthony.l.nguyen@intel.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20250224190647.3601930-2-anthony.l.nguyen@intel.com\nSigned-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\nindex b83f99c01d91..8aabf7749aa5 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -193,10 +194,6 @@ void ice_free_vfs(struct ice_pf *pf)\n \t\t\twr32(hw, GLGEN_VFLRSTAT(reg_idx), BIT(bit_idx));\n \t\t}\n \n-\t\t/* clear malicious info since the VF is getting released */\n-\t\tif (!ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n-\t\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n-\n \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n \t}\n \n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version: \nmodified file: drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n--- workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/newer/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/v6.12-rc7/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -194,8 +194,7 @@\n  \t\t}\n  \n -\t\tif (!ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n +\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n  \n  \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  \t}\n\n""""""\nmodified file: drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n--- workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/newer/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n+++ workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/v6.12-rc7/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n@@ -717,23 +717,6 @@\n  }\n  \n -static void ice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(struct ice_vf *vf)\n -{\n -\tstruct ice_pf *pf = vf->pf;\n -\n -\tif (ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\tice_mbx_vf_clear_cnt_e830(&pf->hw, vf->vf_id);\n -\telse\n -\t\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n -}\n -\n -/**\n   * ice_reset_all_vfs - reset all allocated VFs in one go\n   * @pf: pointer to the PF structure\n   *\n@@ -759,7 +742,7 @@\n  \n  \tice_for_each_vf(pf, bkt, vf)\n -\t\tice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(vf);\n +\t\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  \tif (test_and_set_bit(ICE_VF_DIS, pf->state)) {\n@@ -975,7 +958,7 @@\n  \tice_eswitch_update_repr(&vf->repr_id, vsi);\n  \n -\tice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(vf);\n +\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  out_unlock:\n  \tif (lag && lag->bonded && lag->primary &&\n@@ -1028,10 +1011,7 @@\n  \tice_vf_fdir_init(vf);\n  \n -\tif (ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\tice_mbx_vf_clear_cnt_e830(&pf->hw, vf->vf_id);\n -\telse\n -\t\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n +\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  \tmutex_init(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  }\n\n""""""\n\n""""""\n\n===end==='}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please return the final result.'}], 'response': 'A. Commit message:\nice: Fix deinitializing VF in error path for older kernel version\n\nB. Change summary:\nThe patch moves the removal of VFs from the snapshot PF-VF mailbox list to the `ice_free_vf_entries()` function, ensuring that VFs are properly removed even in error paths. This prevents potential list corruption and use-after-free bugs when enabling SR-IOV VFs.\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nMedium\n\nD. Fixed Code:\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\nindex 8aabf7749aa5..c0d3e1a2b4c6 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -194,7 +194,6 @@\n  \t\t}\n  \n  \t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n-\n  \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  \t}\n  }\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\nindex e830abcd1234..f0d3e1a2b4c6 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n@@ -975,7 +975,7 @@\n  \tice_eswitch_update_repr(&vf->repr_id, vsi);\n  \n-\tice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(vf);\n+\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  out_unlock:\n  \tif (lag && lag->bonded && lag->primary &&\n@@ -1028,10 +1028,7 @@\n  \tice_vf_fdir_init(vf);\n  \n-\tif (ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n-\t\tice_mbx_vf_clear_cnt_e830(&pf->hw, vf->vf_id);\n-\telse\n-\t\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n+\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  \tmutex_init(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  }', 'request_token': 0, 'response_token': 0}]
